id: pm-v2pg4f
title: Prevent stale cleanup from reclaiming a lock during owner metadata initialization
description: "A lock file becomes visible at exclusive open before owner JSON is written. Concurrent automatic stale recovery classifies the empty file as stale and can unlink a live creator, granting overlapping owners and losing telemetry counter updates. Coordinate initialization with the existing stale-cleanup gate."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-14T13:17:30.265Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-14T13:52:02.888Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-14T13:52:01.990Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-14T13:52:01.990Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A deterministic paused owner-write interleaving never grants a second owner; failed initialization cleans its own lock safely; real multi-process telemetry retains every counter transition and one installation identity; existing stale recovery and exact coverage remain green.
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: Fence exclusive lock creation and owner metadata publication with the existing stale-cleanup coordination gate; clean failed initialization safely
expected_result: A concurrent stale reader cannot acquire a live initializing lock or lose serialized telemetry counter transitions
actual_result: Deterministic pre-fix overlap now refused; failed initialization retry passes; 66 linked tests and 8871 full-suite tests pass at exact four-metric 100 percent coverage
component: core/lock
