comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-14T13:17:30.265Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status 2759-item export plus current newly created delivery items, request-specific lock initialization search, open/in-progress inventories, and full pm-zwib/pm-lvyd context inspected. pm-zwib covers two stale waiters replacing valid metadata; this distinct empty-owner initialization window is not covered. Real four-process sampler lost one ordinal under the existing mutex."
  "2026-09-14T13:24:44.145Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: pausing the first exclusive-open owner write deterministically granted an overlapping second owner before the fix. Lock creation now holds the same token-validated coordination gate as stale cleanup and release, including removal of its own failed initialization. The original warning-token regression still injects EACCES on lock metadata; unrelated gate-owner reads remain real. Focused validation passed 17 files / 199 tests, including real multi-process sampler counts and collector lifecycle/identity assertions."
  "2026-09-14T13:50:37.075Z","harness:codex","Final validation: linked lock and real multiprocess telemetry selection passed 66 tests; full suite passed 8871 tests with exact statements/branches/functions/lines coverage 100/100/100/100. SDK import and CLI transport budgets pass. Source initialization safety is complete and prepared for hosted review; the separate thousand-agent throughput item remains a future workload."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-14T13:25:16.135Z","harness:codex",Exclusive file creation alone does not publish valid owner metadata atomically. A stale reader must share the same coordination gate as initialization and release. Test the empty-file publication window with explicit synchronization rather than timing sleeps.
